<title>INDIA: Indian banks closed for religious holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian banks closed for religious holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian banks are closed to observe a religious holiday on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The call money market is inactive. The market closed in the 3.0 pct to 3.5 pct range on Saturday, the last working day.</p>
<p>Normal market activity is expected to resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay nmewsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
